@h1 CLI reference h1@

The complete command-line contract: five subcommands, every flag, exit codes,
diagnostics, and environment variables. Source:
@code packages/cli/src/*.ts code@.

@h2 Synopsis h2@

@@@pre
wit parse <file>
wit check <file>
wit fmt <file> [-w|--write]
wit build <file> [-o out.html|out.md|out.pdf] [--format html|md|pdf] [--raw | --fragment]
                  [--sources wit.sources.json --allow-exec] [--env .env]
wit tour <file>
wit --version | --help
pre@@@

@aside(class note)
@strong Version drift: strong@ the code constant is @code VERSION = '0.1.0' code@
(printed by @code wit --version code@), but a @code v0.2.0 code@ git tag exists.
This page quotes the constant and flags the gap — see
@a |href /docs/reference/limitations/| limitations a@.

aside@

@h2 Global h2@

@table |rows [[Invocation, Result, Exit], [wit --help or -h, usage text, 0], [wit --version or -v, prints 0.1.0, 0], [unknown command, help on stderr, 2]]| |caption Global flags| table@

@h2 wit parse h2@

Parse a file and print its AST as pretty JSON. @strong No flags. strong@

@table |rows [[Outcome, Exit], [prints AST JSON, 0], [parse error — diagnostic on stderr, 1], [missing file argument, 2]]| |caption parse| table@

@h2 wit check h2@

Parse @strong and strong@ resolve — a fast validity check. @strong No flags.
strong@ Does @strong not strong@ expand or render; catches resolve-stage errors
only.

@table |rows [[Outcome, Exit], [clean — prints ok and the path, 0], [any stage error, 1], [missing file argument, 2]]| |caption check| table@

@h2 wit fmt h2@

Structural re-indent. Prints to stdout by default.

@table |rows [[Flag, Meaning, Default], [-w or --write, write in place; prints formatted or unchanged, stdout], [parse error, nothing written; exit 1, —]]| |caption fmt| table@

Preserves prose exactly and leaves raw double-at bodies, scripts, record and
data values, and form-fill bodies verbatim. Missing file argument → exit 2.

@h2 wit build h2@

The full pipeline: parse → load → resolve → expand → render.

@table |rows [[Flag, Argument, Meaning, Default], [-o or --out, a path, output file; format inferred from extension, stdout], [--format, html or md or pdf, explicit format overriding inference, html], [--fragment, none, bare wit-doc article only, off], [--raw, none, full document with reset-only CSS, off], [--sources, a json file, external-data source config, none], [--env, a dotenv file, merged into the env source and child env, none], [--allow-exec, none, permit running configured source programs, off]]| |caption build flags| table@

@h3 Format inference h3@

@table |rows [[Extension, Format], [.html or .htm, html], [.md or .markdown, md], [.pdf, pdf], [anything else, E_UNKNOWN_OUTPUT_FORMAT — exit 1]]| |caption Output format from extension| table@

@h3 --raw versus --fragment h3@

If both are given, @code --fragment code@ wins: the HTML options return early on
@code fragment code@ before checking @code raw code@. @code --fragment code@
emits @@@code <article class="wit-doc"> code@@@ only; @code --raw code@ emits a
full document with a reset-only base for author-supplied styling; the default is
a self-contained styled document (a Word-like house style).

@h3 PDF specifics h3@

Requires @code -o <file.pdf> code@ (else an error, exit 1). Drives a headless
system Chrome or Chromium (candidate list in the source, or a
@code WIT_CHROME code@ override — the override wins with no fallback). Injects a
@code base href code@ (the document directory) so relative assets resolve; runs
with a 60-second timeout; writes a temporary HTML then unlinks it. No Chrome →
a helpful error, exit 1. Success → prints the written path.

@h2 wit tour h2@

An indented AST tree plus an AST-coverage report.

@table |rows [[Flag, Meaning], [--report, force report mode even on a non-TTY], [--no-report, tree only — for piping], [default, report on a TTY]]| |caption tour| table@

The footer reports @code AST kinds seen: X/Y code@ against the 24 known kinds,
plus the @code paramsSource code@ variants and @code NodeDef code@ shapes seen.
Overridable by @code WIT_TOUR_REPORT=1 code@ / @code WIT_TOUR_NO_REPORT=1 code@.
Unknown flag → exit 2. Checked output lives in
@code tests/integration/feature-tour.tour.txt code@.

@h2 Cross-cutting h2@

@table |rows [[Exit code, Meaning], [0, success], [1, stage or IO error], [2, usage error]]| |caption Exit codes| table@

@table |rows [[Env var, Effect], [WIT_CHROME, PDF browser override — no fallback], [WIT_DEBUG_COMMENTS=1, keep comments in the HTML render], [WIT_TOUR_REPORT / WIT_TOUR_NO_REPORT, force tour report mode]]| |caption Environment variables| table@

All diagnostics use @@@code file:line:col: E_CODE: message code@@@. See the
@a |href /docs/reference/errors/| error catalogue a@.

